SMP timeout: restore panic (default ON) so the fixed panic-dump actually runs.

0155 removed the panic() on a secondary bring-up timeout, replacing it with a
graceful DROPPED+continue so "the boot reaches userspace and the SWEETLOG
flusher writes the diagnostics".  0156 then stopped publishing SMP when any
CPU was dropped.  On hardware BOTH log paths ended up dead:

  * sweet_panic_log_dump() is called ONLY from sweet_pe_halt_restart(), i.e.
    only on panic().  0155 removed the SMP panic => the dump (just fixed by
    0157 with cached GPT geometry + kick_always) NEVER runs.
  * the alternative flusher starts only after root mount (sweet_emmc_extras_start
    in onc_emmc_init); with CPUs dropped the boot dies ~58 s in, before root
    mount => the flusher NEVER runs either.
  * normal sweetrebootat would reach PEHaltRestart via reboot_kernel(), but it
    is set to 960 s while the phone resets at ~58 s through another path.
  Result: 11D..11L plus 11M all decoded to the SAME stale seq=44 SWEETLOG,
  and the misc partition was entirely zero -- no dump was ever attempted.

0158 (iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetCPU.cpp, SMP startup-timeout branch only):
  - a boot arg `sweetpaniconfail` (DEFAULT 1) restores panic() right after the
    full diagnostic IOLog, so console ring already holds every GIC/SGI line;
  - `sweetpaniconfail=0` keeps 0155's graceful drop for A/B.

Safety: the reset hook is installed in arm_init() BEFORE IOKit/SMP
(0143, sweet_early_reset_install) and 0146 already cleared the Android BCB
there, so this panic goes sweet_pe_halt_restart() -> 0157 dump -> WDT reset ->
ABL sees cleared BCB -> boot=TWRP.  The unattended loop then decodes a FRESH
SWEETLOG with the complete startup-timeout + GIC readback + SGI debug text.

This reverses only 0155's "no panic" decision on the failure path; the SMP
bring-up sequence, 0153 GIC frames, 0157 dump fix are untouched.  Next patch
number after this is 0159.
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetCPU.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetCPU.cpp
@@ -639,7 +639,42 @@
 				 * full mark/stage/GICC readback lines) to the userdata
 				 * tail, the BCB has been cleared, and the next
 				 * unattended cycle reads the whole thing back.
+				 *
+				 * 0158: that assumption proved false on hardware --
+				 * the boot dies ~58 s later, before root mount, so the
+				 * flusher never starts either and BOTH log paths end up
+				 * dead (9 consecutive stale SWEETLOGs, misc all zero).
+				 * Default to a panic here so the 0157-fixed
+				 * sweet_panic_log_dump() actually runs: the halt hook is
+				 * installed in arm_init() BEFORE SMP and 0146 already
+				 * cleared the BCB there, so the panic dumps the console
+				 * ring (holding all the lines above) and resets to TWRP.
+				 * sweetpaniconfail=0 restores the graceful drop.
 				 */
+				{
+					uint32_t pcf = 1;
+
+					if (!PE_parse_boot_argn("sweetpaniconfail",
+					    &pcf, sizeof(pcf)) || pcf != 0) {
+						panic("SWEET CPU: cpu=%u startup "
+						    "timeout (0158) target=0x%llx "
+						    "entry=0x%llx rc=%d aff=%d/%d/%d "
+						    "mark=0x%llx stage=0x%llx "
+						    "init=%u sig=%u sig_raw=0x%08x",
+						    i,
+						    (unsigned long long)psci_target,
+						    (unsigned long long)psci_entry,
+						    (int)psci_rc, (int)aff_before,
+						    (int)aff_after, (int)aff_again,
+						    (unsigned long long)mark,
+						    (unsigned long long)stage,
+						    (unsigned)__atomic_load_n(
+						    &cpu->initialized,
+						    __ATOMIC_ACQUIRE),
+						    (unsigned)sweet_cpu_signal_is_enabled(i),
+						    (unsigned)sig_raw);
+					}
+				}
 				IOLog("SWEET CPU: cpu=%u DROPPED after timeout; "
 				    "continuing the boot so the log reaches eMMC\n", i);
 				sweet_smp_dropped++;
